Wanda (REL1_46): UTF-8-safe truncation of the LLM context

Problem: generateLLMResponse() cuts the wiki/Cargo context with substr() to a byte
budget. If the cut lands inside a multibyte UTF-8 character (e.g. German umlauts),
the string becomes invalid UTF-8, json_encode() returns false and an empty body is
sent to the LLM -> OpenAI "HTTP 400: We could not parse the JSON body".

Fix:
 - substr() -> mb_strcut( ..., 'UTF-8' ) where text sent to the LLM is truncated
   (same byte budget, never cuts inside a character)
 - JSON_INVALID_UTF8_SUBSTITUTE on all outgoing request payloads as a safety net
   for invalid UTF-8 already present in page/PDF text

Based on: wikimedia/mediawiki-extensions-Wanda REL1_46 @ f05813795b1d
Apply in the extension directory: patch -p1 < wanda-utf8-truncation.patch

